    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "The non-terminating decimal among the following fractions is: 25/16, 29/4, 31/3, 41/5 &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;: 25/16, 29/4, 31/3, 41/5",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The non-terminating decimal among the following fractions is:</p><p>25/16, 29/4, 31/3, 41/5 </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2357;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;:</p><p>25/16, 29/4, 31/3, 41/5 </p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "29/4 29/4",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">29/4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">29/4</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "31/3 31/3",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">31/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31/3</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "25/16 25/16",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">25/16</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">25/16</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "41/5 41/5",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">41/5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">41/5</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><b>[If the denominator of a rational number has either 2 or 5 or both as prime factors, then the decimal expansion is terminating decimal]</b></p><p>25/16, factors of 16 is 2 * 2 * 2 * 2, so it is a terminating decimal.</p><p>29/4, factors of 4 is 2 * 2, so it is a terminating decimal. </p><p>31/3, factors of 3 is 3, so it is a non - terminating decimal.</p><p>41/5, factors of 5 is 5, so it is a terminating decimal.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "The denominator of a fraction is 5 more than the numerator. When both increased by 4 the fraction becomes 4/5. Find the new fraction obtained when original fraction got multiplied by 3/2. &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 4 &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 4/5 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 3/2 &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2344;&#2312; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The denominator of a fraction is 5 more than the numerator. When both increased by 4 the fraction becomes 4/5. Find the new fraction obtained when original fraction got multiplied by 3/2.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 4 &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 4/5 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 3/2 &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2344;&#2312; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "3/4 3/4",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">3/4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/4</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2/3 2/3",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/3</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "5/7 5/7",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">5/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5/7</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "8/7 8/7",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">8/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8/7</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Let the original fraction be x/(x + 5)</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(x + 4)/(x + 9) = 4/5</p><p>5x + 20 = 4x + 36</p><p>x = 16</p><p>original fraction = 16/21</p><p>new obtained fraction = 16/21 * 3/2 = 8/7</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "Which of the following numbers is the terminating decimal? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following numbers is the terminating decimal?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
