    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q15",
      "number": 15,
      "question": "Which of the following is true? I. 0.2 59 = 128/495 II. 0. 42 = 7/15 &#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;? I. 0.2 59 = 128/495 II. 0. 42 = 7/15",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is true?</p><p>I. 0.2<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">59</span> = 128/495</p><p>II. 0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">42</span> = 7/15</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366;/&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p>I. 0.2<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">59</span> = 128/495</p><p>II. 0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">42</span> = 7/15</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Only II &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Both I and II I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Both I and II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Only I &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Neither I nor II &#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Neither I nor II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><b>From I: </b>Let x<b> = </b>0.25959...</p><p>Then, 10x = 2.5959..</p><p>1000x = 259.5959..</p><p>1000x  -  10x = 257</p><p>990x = 257</p><p>x = 257/990</p><p>Hence, statement I is false.</p><p><b>From II: </b>Let y = 0.4242...</p><p>Then, 100y = 42.4242..</p><p>100y  -  y = 42</p><p>y = 42/99 = 14/33&#8800; 7/15</p><p>Hence, statement II is false.</p><p></p><p><b>Express Method </b></p><p>From I: X = (259 - 2)/990 = 257/990</p><p>Hence statement I is false.</p><p></p><p>From II: Y = 42/99 = 14/33 which is not equal to 7/15.</p><p>Hence statement II is false.</p><p></p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q16",
      "number": 16,
      "question": "When a fraction is multiplied by the square of &radic;5/2, then it becomes 1(1/3). If numerator of the fraction is increased by 50% and its denominator is decreased by 20%, then the resultant is __. &#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &radic;5/2 &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; 1(1/3) &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 50% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350; ______ &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>When a fraction is multiplied by the square of &radic;5/2, then it becomes 1(1/3). If numerator of the fraction is increased by 50% and its denominator is decreased by 20%, then the resultant is __.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &radic;5/2 &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; 1(1/3) &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 50% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350; ______ &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "5/2 5/2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">5/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5/2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2 2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4 4",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "7/3 7/3",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">7/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7/3</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>1(1/3) means (1 + 1/3) or (4/3).</p><p>Let the fraction = p/q</p><p>Then, (&radic;5/2)<sup>2</sup> * p/q = 4/3</p><p>p/q = (4/3) * 4/5 = 16/15</p><p>now, when numerator of the fraction is increased by 50% and its denominator is decreased by 20%, then resultant = ((100 + 50)% of 16)/((100  -  20)% of 15)</p><p>= (150 * 16)/(80 * 15)</p><p>= <b>2</b></p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q17",
      "number": 17,
      "question": "Which of the following is largest among the fractions 8/9, 11/12, 23/24 and 31/36? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;- 8/9, 11/12, 23/24 &#2324;&#2352; 31/36 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is largest among the fractions 8/9, 11/12, 23/24 and 31/36?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;- 8/9, 11/12, 23/24 &#2324;&#2352; 31/36 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "11/12 11/12",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">11/12</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">11/12</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "8/9 8/9",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">8/9</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">8/9</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "31/36 31/36",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">31/36</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">31/36</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "23/24 23/24",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">23/24</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">23/24</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>To find the largest among the given fractions, we have to find out the LCM of their denominators.</p><p>LCM of 9, 12, 24 and 36 = 72</p><p>Now, the fraction becomes,</p><p>(8 x 8)/72 = 64/72</p><p>(11 x 6)/72 = 66/72</p><p>(23 x 3)/72 = 69/72 (largest)</p><p>(31 x 2)/72 = 62/72</p><p>Therefore, 23/24 is largest among given four fractions.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q18",
      "number": 18,
      "question": "The denominator of a fraction is 5 more than its numerator, which is a positive integer. The numerator is doubled and the denominator is now 3. The resultant fraction is 20/9 more than the original fraction. What is the numerator of the original fraction? &#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2348; &#2361;&#2352; 3 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 20/9 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The denominator of a fraction is 5 more than its numerator, which is a positive integer. The numerator is doubled and the denominator is now 3. The resultant fraction is 20/9 more than the original fraction. What is the numerator of the original fraction?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2348; &#2361;&#2352; 3 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 20/9 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1 1",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2 2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4 4",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "5 5",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Let the numerator = n, then denominator = n+5. Hence the fraction = n/(n+5)</p> <p>According to the given condition, 2n/3  -  n/(n+5) = 20/9</p> <p>Multiplying all terms by 9(n+5) [LCM of denominators]</p> <p>6n(n+5)  -  9n = 20(n+5)</p> <p>=&gt; 6n<sup>2</sup> + 30n  -  9n = 20n + 100</p> <p>=&gt; 6n<sup>2</sup> + n  -  100 = 0</p> <p>=&gt; 6n<sup>2</sup> + 25n  -  24n  -  100 = 0</p> <p>=&gt; n(6n+25)  -  4(6n+25) = 0</p> <p>=&gt; (6n+25)(n-4) = 0</p> <p>Since n is a positive integer, n =4</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
