      "id": "7550a3c8ff42-q19",
      "number": 19,
      "question": "If we add 1 to the twice of the denominator of a fraction then we will get 1/5. If we subtract 1 from numerator and add 1 to denominator then we will get 1/4. What is the original fraction? &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2361;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2325;&#2379; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2361;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1/5 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2361;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2361;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1/4 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If we add 1 to the twice of the denominator of a fraction then we will get 1/5. If we subtract 1 from numerator and add 1 to denominator then we will get 1/4. What is the original fraction?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2361;&#2350; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2325;&#2379; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2340;&#2379; &#2361;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1/5 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2361;&#2350; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 1 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2361;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 1/4 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "1/2 1/2",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1/2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/2</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2/7 2/7",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">2/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/7</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "1/3 1/3",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">1/3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1/3</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "3/7 3/7",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">3/7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3/7</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Let the fraction = m/n</p><p>According to the 1<sup>st</sup> condition; m/(2n+1) = 1/5</p><p>=&gt;5m = 2n + 1</p><p>=&gt; 5m  -  2n = 1 ... (1)</p><p>According to the 2<sup>nd</sup> condition; (m-1)/(n+ 1) = 1/4</p><p>=&gt;4m - 4 = n +1</p><p>=&gt; 4m - n = 5 ...(2)</p><p>Solving (1) and (2) we will get; m = 3 and n = 7</p><p>Hence the original fraction = m/n = 3/7</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
